faq:
  - q: I'm already in individual therapy. Can I do both?
    a: Individual therapy and group work can run alongside each other. For some people, group work can offer a supportive space alongside their individual therapy; for others, it can be a good starting point on its own.
  - q: How many people are in a group, and how long does it last?
    a: Depending on the type of group, usually between 6 and 12 people. Sessions are held once a week and last 90 to 120 minutes.
  - q: Will there be groups in English?
    a: Yes. Turkish and English groups run separately. If you would like to join an English group, just mention it when you get in touch.
  - q: Do I have to tell my story in the group?
    a: No. You decide how much you share. In some sessions, simply listening is also a way of taking part.
