        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink mb-6">What is group work?</h2>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">Group work means a few people who are struggling with, or interested in, a similar issue meeting regularly with a psychologist. The topic is set from the start: sleep, anxiety, parenting, exam periods, anger. Everyone's story is different, but the interest or the difficulty can be shared.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-8">Each session has a topic, a structure and sometimes an exercise to try between sessions.</p>
        <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
          <div class="bg-warm rounded-2xl p-6 border border-warm-tertiary">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-2">Opens the topic</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">The psychologist leads the group and opens each session's topic.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-warm rounded-2xl p-6 border border-warm-tertiary">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-2">Does the exercises together</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Exercises in the session are done together with the group.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-warm rounded-2xl p-6 border border-warm-tertiary">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-2">Keeps it safe</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Makes sure the work stays safe for everyone.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-16 bg-warm">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-5 lg:px-8">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink mb-6">Famagusta is a small town. How is confidentiality protected?</h2>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">This is almost everyone's first question about group work, and you are right to ask it.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">Every group begins with a confidentiality agreement: what is said in the room stays in the room. This rule is discussed in the first session and repeated in every session.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">You decide how much you share. Joining a group does not mean you have to tell your story. In some sessions, simply listening is also a way of taking part.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-16 bg-white">
